        "original_id": "d1ea7852-7d52-58cf-9847-eae7e2cb9013",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Vinessa Shaw, Stanley Kubrick, Wes Craven, Josh Hartnett, Arthur Schnitzler, Nicole Kidman, Tom Cruise\n- Works: Ladybugs, Eyes Wide Shut, The Hills Have Eyes, 40 Days and 40 Nights, Traumnovelle\n- Topics: filmography, adaptations, settings\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Schnitzler wrote the 1926 novella Traumnovelle, also translated as Dream Story.\n- Eyes Wide Shut is based on Arthur Schnitzler's 1926 novella Traumnovelle.\n- Eyes Wide Shut transfers its story setting from early 20th century Vienna to 1990s New York City.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in the film Ladybugs in 1992.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in Stanley Kubrick's film Eyes Wide Shut in 1999.\n- Nicole Kidman worked with Tom Cruise again on Stanley Kubrick's erotic thriller Eyes Wide Shut in 1999.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in 40 Days and 40 Nights as the sadistic ex-girlfriend of Josh Hartnett's character.\n- Vinessa Shaw appeared in the 2006 remake of Wes Craven's horror film The Hills Have Eyes.",
